searchData={"items":[{"type":"module","title":"MedCore","doc":"Pure functional clinical signal and live-session domain core for MedEx.\n\nDefines stream contracts, live session state, preview vs. recording integrity\ntypes, product profile behaviours, and deterministic state-machine seams.","ref":"MedCore.html"},{"type":"function","title":"MedCore.version/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.html#version/0"},{"type":"behaviour","title":"MedCore.Profile","doc":"Behaviour implemented by clinical product applications to compose MedEx\ntransport archetypes, streams, inference hooks, and device control policies.","ref":"MedCore.Profile.html"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.Profile.inference_hook/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Profile.html#t:inference_hook/0"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.Profile.topology/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Profile.html#t:topology/0"},{"type":"callback","title":"MedCore.Profile.control_policy/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Profile.html#c:control_policy/0"},{"type":"callback","title":"MedCore.Profile.inference_hooks/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Profile.html#c:inference_hooks/0"},{"type":"callback","title":"MedCore.Profile.streams/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Profile.html#c:streams/0"},{"type":"callback","title":"MedCore.Profile.topology/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Profile.html#c:topology/0"},{"type":"module","title":"MedCore.Session","doc":"Immutable live clinical transport session aggregate and pure reducer (`step/2`).\n\nA `Session` owns live participants, WebRTC connection attempts (`connection_id`),\ntransient preview interruptions, independent recording continuity, and device\nacquisitions (`acquisition_id`). It can outlast individual browser reconnects\nand supports standalone capture with `encounter_ref: nil` and no connected peer.","ref":"MedCore.Session.html"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.Session.acquisition_id/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Session.html#t:acquisition_id/0"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.Session.connection_id/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Session.html#t:connection_id/0"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.Session.continuity_state/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Session.html#t:continuity_state/0"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.Session.effect/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Session.html#t:effect/0"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.Session.encounter_ref/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Session.html#t:encounter_ref/0"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.Session.event/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Session.html#t:event/0"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.Session.integrity_report/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Session.html#t:integrity_report/0"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.Session.integrity_subject/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Session.html#t:integrity_subject/0"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.Session.session_id/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Session.html#t:session_id/0"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.Session.t/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.Session.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"function","title":"MedCore.Session.new/1","doc":"Constructs a new live clinical session. `encounter_ref` is optional (`nil` for standalone capture).","ref":"MedCore.Session.html#new/1"},{"type":"function","title":"MedCore.Session.step/2","doc":"Pure state transition function `{next_session, effects} = step(session, event)`.","ref":"MedCore.Session.html#step/2"},{"type":"module","title":"MedCore.StreamSpec","doc":"Declarative contract for a clinical media, telemetry, or device control stream.","ref":"MedCore.StreamSpec.html"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.StreamSpec.archetype/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.StreamSpec.html#t:archetype/0"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.StreamSpec.integrity_policy/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.StreamSpec.html#t:integrity_policy/0"},{"type":"type","title":"MedCore.StreamSpec.t/0","doc":"","ref":"MedCore.StreamSpec.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"module","title":"MedRTC","doc":"OTP effect shell and WebRTC/Opus/SCTP runtime boundary for MedEx.\n\nOrchestrates live session coordination (`MedRTC.SessionServer`) and WebRTC\npeer negotiation (`MedRTC.PeerLoopback`) while delegating pure clinical signal\ninvariants to `MedCore.Session`.","ref":"MedRTC.html"},{"type":"module","title":"MedRTC.PeerLoopback","doc":"Minimal real `ExWebRTC.PeerConnection` SDP/ICE loopback harness used to\nexercise live WebRTC negotiation, peer disconnect, and replacement connection\nestablishment against `MedRTC.SessionServer`.","ref":"MedRTC.PeerLoopback.html"},{"type":"type","title":"MedRTC.PeerLoopback.negotiated_pair/0","doc":"","ref":"MedRTC.PeerLoopback.html#t:negotiated_pair/0"},{"type":"function","title":"MedRTC.PeerLoopback.close_pair/1","doc":"Closes both `ExWebRTC.PeerConnection` processes in a negotiated pair.","ref":"MedRTC.PeerLoopback.html#close_pair/1"},{"type":"function","title":"MedRTC.PeerLoopback.connect_pair/2","doc":"Starts two real `ExWebRTC.PeerConnection` instances with an `:audio`\ntransceiver, exchanges SDP offer/answer and ICE candidates, and waits until\nboth peers reach `:connected`.","ref":"MedRTC.PeerLoopback.html#connect_pair/2"},{"type":"module","title":"MedRTC.SessionServer","doc":"OTP `GenServer` owning a live `%MedCore.Session{}` and dispatching emitted\nproducer facts to registered subscribers.","ref":"MedRTC.SessionServer.html"},{"type":"type","title":"MedRTC.SessionServer.start_opt/0","doc":"","ref":"MedRTC.SessionServer.html#t:start_opt/0"},{"type":"function","title":"MedRTC.SessionServer.child_spec/1","doc":"Returns a specification to start this module under a supervisor.\n\nSee `Supervisor`.","ref":"MedRTC.SessionServer.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","title":"MedRTC.SessionServer.dispatch/2","doc":"","ref":"MedRTC.SessionServer.html#dispatch/2"},{"type":"function","title":"MedRTC.SessionServer.snapshot/1","doc":"","ref":"MedRTC.SessionServer.html#snapshot/1"},{"type":"function","title":"MedRTC.SessionServer.start_link/1","doc":"","ref":"MedRTC.SessionServer.html#start_link/1"},{"type":"module","title":"MedWeb","doc":"Reusable Phoenix signaling contract (`MedWeb.Signaling`) and shipped browser\n`RTCPeerConnection` hook assets for MedEx live sessions.","ref":"MedWeb.html"},{"type":"module","title":"MedWeb.Signaling","doc":"Browser signaling message normalization and reconnect handshake contract for\nMedEx live sessions.","ref":"MedWeb.Signaling.html"},{"type":"type","title":"MedWeb.Signaling.client_signal/0","doc":"","ref":"MedWeb.Signaling.html#t:client_signal/0"},{"type":"function","title":"MedWeb.Signaling.hook_asset_full_path/0","doc":"Resolves the absolute path to the shipped browser hook asset whether loaded\nfrom `:med_web` in source mode or from the Welded `:med_ex` SDK package.","ref":"MedWeb.Signaling.html#hook_asset_full_path/0"},{"type":"function","title":"MedWeb.Signaling.hook_asset_path/0","doc":"Returns the shipped browser hook asset relative path inside `priv/`.","ref":"MedWeb.Signaling.html#hook_asset_path/0"},{"type":"function","title":"MedWeb.Signaling.to_session_event/1","doc":"Normalizes a browser signaling event into a pure `MedCore.Session` event.","ref":"MedWeb.Signaling.html#to_session_event/1"},{"type":"extras","title":"Overview","doc":"# MedEx\n\n`MedEx` is a reusable Elixir/Phoenix/LiveView/WebRTC/Opus SDK poncho for connected medical devices.\n\nInstead of building a leaky \"generic video call\" wrapper, `MedEx` inverts the typical WebRTC architecture: **clinical signal integrity, multi-stream time alignment, lossless capture continuity, and audited device control are the core domain**, while WebRTC, Opus, RTP, and SCTP are pluggable transports that serve those invariants.\n\nThis repository is a non-umbrella Elixir poncho workspace orchestrated with [Blitz](https://github.com/nshkrdotcom/blitz) and [Weld](https://github.com/nshkrdotcom/weld). The root `mix.exs` (`:med_ex_workspace`) is a tooling-only project that coordinates parallel child checks and projects the consumable `:med_ex` SDK artifact.\n\n---","ref":"readme.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Ownership Boundary (med_ex SDK vs. med_fabric Product Platform) - Overview","doc":"`MedEx` owns the **reusable real-time clinical signal, live session, WebRTC/Opus/Membrane transport, browser media workbench, and opt-in live signal-compute plane**.\n\nDurable clinical encounters, clinician observation acceptance, transactional outbox persistence, HL7 FHIR delivery, and full clinical product applications live in the companion `med_fabric` workspace (`mf_domain`, `mf_runtime`, `mf_store`, `mf_interop`, `apps/exam`). Dependencies flow strictly one-way (`med_fabric` → `:med_ex`), while `med_ex` remains usable standalone without requiring an external `encounter_ref`.\n\n- **Single SDK Distribution Identity (`:med_ex`)**: Downstream consumers such as `med_fabric/apps/exam` depend on **one OTP app (`:med_ex`)** projected by Weld from `core/med_core`, `core/med_rtc`, and `core/med_web` (an explicitly browser-capable default SDK). `core/med_adapters` stays an opt-in source project excluded from the default projection until a concrete consumer proves compatibility against `:med_ex`'s public API; a separate headless-only SDK distribution waits for an actual headless consumer.\n- **Minimal Reference App (`apps/med_pulse`)**: Proves standalone consumption of `med_ex`'s public API (two-browser WebRTC call + deterministic simulated capture + preview disconnect/rejoin + duplicate completion handling). Full clinical product roadmaps belong in `med_fabric`.\n- **`MedCore.Session`** (`session_id`) outlasts individual WebRTC peer connections (`connection_id`), tracks standalone or encounter-linked captures (`acquisition_id`), and separates **live preview integrity** (`{:preview_stream, id}`) from **recording artifact integrity** (`{:recording_artifact, acquisition_id}`). See the canonical reconnect trace in [core/med_core/README.md](core/med_core/README.md).\n\n---","ref":"readme.html#ownership-boundary-med_ex-sdk-vs-med_fabric-product-platform"},{"type":"extras","title":"Poncho Architecture & Package Map - Overview","doc":"```text\nmed_ex/\n├── mix.exs                         # Tooling root (:med_ex_workspace) with Blitz + Weld\n├── build_support/weld.exs          # Weld manifest projecting the browser-capable :med_ex SDK\n├── core/\n│   ├── med_core/                   # Pure functional core (zero OTP, zero IO, 100% deterministic)\n│   ├── med_rtc/                    # OTP effect runtime, supervision tree, ExWebRTC/ExSCTP/Membrane shell\n│   ├── med_web/                    # Reusable Phoenix Signaling, LiveComponents, JS WebAudio/WebRTC hooks\n│   └── med_adapters/               # Opt-in source project: signal/AI & external media ports (Ortex, NeuroKit2/WFDB, LiveKit, Pipecat)\n└── apps/\n    └── med_pulse/                  # Minimal standalone SDK reference app\n```","ref":"readme.html#poncho-architecture-package-map"},{"type":"extras","title":"Sub-Package Documentation - Overview","doc":"| Package | Path | Layer | Role | Documentation |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **MedCore** | `core/med_core` | Pure Functional Core *(in `:med_ex` SDK)* | Clinical contracts (`StreamSpec`, `Session`, `Profile`), preview vs. recording integrity model, canonical reconnect trace, and 5 deterministic state machines (`SignalIntegrity`, `TimelineAligner`, `ControlInterlock`, `DegradationPolicy`, `AuditChain`) | [core/med_core/README.md](core/med_core/README.md) |\n| **MedRTC** | `core/med_rtc` | OTP Runtime & Transport Shell *(in `:med_ex` SDK)* | Per-session `:rest_for_one` supervision, `EffectInterpreter`, `ExWebRTC`/`ExSCTP`/`Membrane` pipelines, lossless capture tees, `Rel` TURN/STUN config, and DTLS key pinning | [core/med_rtc/README.md](core/med_rtc/README.md) |\n| **MedWeb** | `core/med_web` | Phoenix & LiveView Workbench *(in `:med_ex` SDK)* | Signed session tokens, WebRTC signaling channel, reusable LiveComponents, WebAudio `AudioWorklet` hooks, and `ex_webrtc_dashboard` metrics | [core/med_web/README.md](core/med_web/README.md) |\n| **MedAdapters** | `core/med_adapters` | Opt-in Signal & Media Ports *(excluded from default SDK)* | `@behaviour` contracts and isolated adapters for in-BEAM ONNX (`Ortex`/`Nx`), Python biosignal workers (`NeuroKit2`, `wfdb-python`), `LiveKit`, and `Pipecat`/`whisper.cpp` | [core/med_adapters/README.md](core/med_adapters/README.md) |\n| **MedPulse** | `apps/med_pulse` | Minimal SDK Reference App | Standalone proof exercising live WebRTC talkback, deterministic simulated capture, preview disconnect/rejoin, and independent recording integrity through `med_ex`'s public API | [apps/med_pulse/README.md](apps/med_pulse/README.md) |\n\n---","ref":"readme.html#sub-package-documentation"},{"type":"extras","title":"4 Orthogonal Clinical Transport Archetypes (Generalizing All 12 Use Cases) - Overview","doc":"Forcing all 12 connected-medical-device use cases through a single \"WebRTC Room\" abstraction breaks clinical safety: browser AEC/NS/AGC ruins digital stethoscope heart sounds; ECG waveforms must never pass through a lossy audio codec; conversational medical voice AI needs full-duplex VAD barge-in rather than multi-peer video fan-out.\n\n`MedEx` decomposes all 12 use cases into **4 composable Clinical Transport Archetypes**. A product composes archetypes inside one synchronized `MedCore.Session` via `MedCore.Profile`:\n\n| Archetype | Core Signal & Protocol Contract | Optimal WebRTC Topology | Degradation & Safety Rule | Covered Use Cases |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **A. Diagnostic Signal Plane** *(High-Fidelity Biosignal Audio)* | Unprocessed PCM over ordered/partially-reliable SCTP DataChannel **or** high-bitrate validated Opus (`stereo=0; maxaveragebitrate=128000; cbr=1; useinbandfec=1`) with browser `echoCancellation: false`, `noiseSuppression: false`, `autoGainControl: false`. | **Server-Terminated Pipeline** (`ex_webrtc` → `membrane_core`) so the server tees the exact bit-stream to lossless capture, optional ONNX QC/screening, and clinician playback. | If packet loss exceeds policy, clipping occurs, or client fails DSP-off attestation, **flag the affected interval as `:non_diagnostic`** in real time (never silently conceal with PLC; report preview vs. recording integrity separately). | **#1** Digital Stethoscope, **#8** Respiratory/Spirometer Sounds, **#9** Speech Therapy (acoustic assessment), **#11** Hearing Aid Fitting (calibrated audio) |\n| **B. Structured Telemetry & Control Plane** *(Lossless Sensor & Interlock)* | Binary framed waveforms (ECG, SpO₂, PPG, airflow, device diagnostics) on SCTP DataChannels (`ex_sctp`) + **separate** authenticated, nonce-sequenced, ACKed Control DataChannel. | **Star / Hub-and-Spoke** terminated in BEAM (`ex_webrtc` + `ex_sctp`). Control commands are never P2P; the BEAM session is the sole authorization & audit authority. | Telemetry carries monotonic hardware sample counters (exact gap detection); Control channel enforces **deadman timeout + idempotency + state-machine interlocks** before actuating settings. | **#4** RPM (ECG/SpO₂), **#10** Remote Device Troubleshooting, **#11** Hearing Device Parameter Fitting, **#3** & **#7** (vitals channels) |\n| **C. Interactive Clinical Media Plane** *(Human-to-Human A/V + Annotations)* | Adaptive Opus (24–48 kbps, DTX, FEC, AEC/NS/AGC **on**) + H.264/VP8 video (simulcast/SVC) + lightweight JSON/CBOR annotation DataChannel (telestration vectors, freeze-frame markers). | **SFU** (`membrane_rtc_engine` in-BEAM for 2–8 clinicians; optional `livekit` adapter for large cohorts). Never full mesh beyond 2–3 peers due to mobile/EMS uplink limits. | Graceful degradation ladder: drop video resolution → drop video FPS → freeze video / preserve Opus audio + telemetry. Never starve Archetype A/B bandwidth for talking-head video. | **#3** Connected Telehealth, **#6** Remote Ultrasound, **#7** Tele-EMS, **#9** Speech Therapy (articulation video), **#12** Remote Clinical Training |\n| **D. Full-Duplex Conversational AI Plane** *(Streaming Speech-to-Agent)* | Low-latency Opus (16–24 kHz, 20 ms frames) terminated on server → VAD (`silero-vad` via `Ortex`) → streaming ASR (`Bumblebee`/`whisper.cpp`) → deterministic clinical guardrails + LLM → TTS back over Opus RTP. | **Edge-to-Server-Terminated** (`ex_webrtc` + `membrane_opus_plugin`, or bridged to `pipecat` over WebRTC/gRPC). | Barge-in cancellation on VAD speech-start; **hard deterministic escalation router** (red-flag symptoms or confidence drop triggers immediate warm handoff to Archetype C clinician SFU). | **#2** AI Voice Patient Monitoring, **#5** AI Medical Voice Assistants |\n\n---","ref":"readme.html#4-orthogonal-clinical-transport-archetypes-generalizing-all-12-use-cases"},{"type":"extras","title":"Vetted Open-Source GitHub Ecosystem - Overview","doc":"- **WebRTC, Media Pipelines & LiveView (`core/med_rtc`, `core/med_web`)**:\n  - [ExWebRTC](https://github.com/elixir-webrtc/ex_webrtc), [ExSCTP](https://github.com/elixir-webrtc/ex_sctp), [LiveExWebRTC](https://github.com/elixir-webrtc/live_ex_webrtc), [ExWebRTC Recorder](https://github.com/elixir-webrtc/ex_webrtc_recorder), [ExWebRTC Dashboard](https://github.com/elixir-webrtc/ex_webrtc_dashboard), [Rel (TURN/STUN)](https://github.com/elixir-webrtc/rel)\n  - [Membrane Core](https://github.com/membraneframework/membrane_core), [membrane_webrtc_plugin](https://github.com/membraneframework/membrane_webrtc_plugin), [membrane_opus_plugin](https://github.com/membraneframework/membrane_opus_plugin), [membrane_wav_plugin](https://github.com/membraneframework/membrane_wav_plugin), [membrane_rtc_engine](https://github.com/fishjam-dev/membrane_rtc_engine)\n- **Opt-In Signal Compute & External Media (`core/med_adapters`)**:\n  - [Nx](https://github.com/elixir-nx/nx), [Ortex](https://github.com/elixir-nx/ortex), [Bumblebee](https://github.com/elixir-nx/bumblebee), [Silero VAD](https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad)\n  - [Open-Stethoscope](https://github.com/NoahIsARider/open-stethoscope), [NeuroKit2](https://github.com/neuropsychology/NeuroKit), [WFDB-Python](https://github.com/MIT-LCP/wfdb-python)\n  - [Pion WebRTC](https://github.com/pion/webrtc), [Pipecat](https://github.com/pipecat-ai/pipecat), [whisper.cpp](https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp), [LiveKit](https://github.com/livekit/livekit)\n\n---","ref":"readme.html#vetted-open-source-github-ecosystem"},{"type":"extras","title":"Verification & Distribution Pipeline - Overview","doc":"| Stage | Command | What It Proves |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Inner Dev Loop (Source Poncho)** | `mix ci` & `mix monorepo.dialyzer` | Fast parallel child checks across `core/*` and `apps/*` via Blitz with zero projection overhead. |\n| **SDK Artifact Projection** | `mix weld.inspect`, `mix weld.project`, `mix weld.verify` | Projects `core/{med_core, med_rtc, med_web}` into one `:med_ex` OTP app (`dist/monolith/med_ex`), compiles, tests, builds docs, and runs `mix hex.build`. |\n| **Tracked Projection / Release** | `mix weld.release.prepare` & `mix weld.release.track --push` | Publishes the verified `:med_ex` projection onto orphan branch `projection/med_ex` so downstream consumers (`med_fabric/apps/exam`) resolve one `:med_ex` package from private Git (and later Hex) with identical app identity locally via Mix Workspace Ops. |\n\n*(Future Weld optimization: fingerprint inputs—selected sources, dependency locks, manifest, shipped assets, and toolchain inputs—before projection so unchanged local projections can be verified and reused safely while keeping fresh clean-consumer builds for release candidates.)*","ref":"readme.html#verification-distribution-pipeline"},{"type":"extras","title":"Workspace Commands - Overview","doc":"```bash\nmix deps.get\nmix monorepo.deps.get\nmix ci\nmix monorepo.dialyzer\nmix weld.inspect\nmix weld.verify\nmix weld.release.prepare\nmix weld.release.track --push\n```","ref":"readme.html#workspace-commands"},{"type":"extras","title":"Security & Regulatory Boundary - Overview","doc":"WebRTC DTLS-SRTP provides transport encryption in transit, which is necessary but insufficient for HIPAA/FDA compliance. `MedEx` enforces short-lived per-session DTLS certificates, role-scoped signaling tokens, transient RAM-only media by default unless an audited capture command runs, and SaMD advisory envelopes (`advisory_only: true`, `model_sha256`, `signal_quality_score`, `integrity_state`) on all inference outputs.","ref":"readme.html#security-regulatory-boundary"},{"type":"extras","title":"License - Overview","doc":"MIT — see [LICENSE](LICENSE).","ref":"readme.html#license"},{"type":"extras","title":"Changelog","doc":"# Changelog\n\nAll notable changes to the `med_ex` poncho workspace will be documented in this file.\n\n## [0.1.0] - 2026-11-22","ref":"changelog.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Added - Changelog","doc":"- Initialized the `med_ex` non-umbrella Elixir poncho workspace with Blitz and Weld orchestration.\n- Added architecture documentation and skeleton packages under `core/` (`med_core`, `med_rtc`, `med_adapters`, `med_web`) and `apps/` (`med_pulse`).\n- Configured Credo, Dialyxir, ExDoc, custom SVG branding assets, and per-package metadata across every child Mix project.","ref":"changelog.html#added"},{"type":"extras","title":"License","doc":"MIT License\n\nCopyright (c) 2026 nshkrdotcom\n\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\nof this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\nin the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\nto use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\ncopies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\nfurnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\nThe above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\ncopies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\nTHE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\nIMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\nFITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\nAUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\nLIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\nOUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\nSOFTWARE.","ref":"license.html"}],"proglang":"elixir","content_type":"text/markdown","producer":{"name":"ex_doc","version":"0.40.5"}}